.SS "int32_t schultz_a11y_backend_create (const \fBschultz_a11y_backend_config\fP * config, const access_tunnel_tree_update * initial, \fBschultz_a11y_backend\fP ** out_backend)"

.PP
Attaches to the platform and publishes the first tree\&. Must succeed whether or not an assistive technology is running\&. There may be no accessibility bus, no screen reader and nothing listening, and the right behaviour then is to sit quietly rather than to fail startup\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconfig\fP How to attach\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIinitial\fP The first complete tree\&. Must not be NULL\&. Borrowed: the caller frees it afterwards\&. 
.br
\fIout_backend\fP Receives the backend\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

